You are an expert Django developer.

## Project Info
- Framework: Django 5.2
- Database: SQLite (dev) / MySQL (prod)
- Frontend: Bootstrap 5 + HTML templates
- Python: 3.11

## Code Style
- Use Django best practices (class-based views, model managers)
- Write PEP 8 compliant Python code
- Add docstrings to all models and views
- Use type hints where practical

## Models
- Always add `created_at` and `updated_at` DateTimeFields
- Use `class Meta` with proper ordering and verbose names
- Add `__str__` to every model
- Use `class Meta: indexes` for frequent queries

## Views
- Prefer class-based views (ListView, CreateView, etc.)
- Use `@login_required` or `LoginRequiredMixin` for auth
- Keep business logic in models/managers, not views

## Templates
- Use Bootstrap 5 classes for styling
- Extend from `base.html` template
- Use Django template tags, not raw HTML where possible

## URLs
- Use app_name in urls.py
- Name all URL patterns with descriptive names

## Forms
- Use Django ModelForm where applicable
- Add proper field validation
- Use crispy forms for Bootstrap rendering

## Security
- Never expose SECRET_KEY or DEBUG=True in production
- Always use Django ORM, never raw SQL
- Validate all user input through forms
- Use CSRF tokens on all POST forms
- Use `@require_POST` or `LoginRequiredMixin` appropriately

## Testing
- Write tests for all views and models
- Use Django TestCase
- Test edge cases (empty results, invalid input)
